/-!
# `A`-line axis program (`AxisUA6`), part 2: a fine exposure as a `PassOK` step

`fxSt stUp stDn e = stUp; call e; stDn`: the set-up pushes the fine descriptor
`descFine w f a y` onto the fine stack `dF` (computed from the axis descriptor on `dA`,
`SetupS` with the one register `dF`), the exposure `e` (`FineBody6`, forward `eF` or back `eB`),
the tear-down pops it.

**`fxF_ok`** / **`fxB_ok`**: the step computes `blkT (2^f) y a` / `blkT y (2^f) a` on stack `0`
at cost `2 Cs + C₀ cFine w f a y`.
